        "original_id": "ac2862ee-7402-5638-81ab-f5475e134d7e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Barnewall, Patrick Barnewall, James II of England, the third Viscount Barnewall\n- Titles and Families: Viscount Barnewall, Lord Trimlestown, Barnewall family\n- Places and Institutions: County Dublin, Irish House of Commons\n- Events: Creation of Viscount Barnewall, Glorious Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- On 29 June 1646, the title Viscount Barnewall was created for Nicholas Barnewall.\n- Before receiving the title Viscount Barnewall, Nicholas Barnewall had represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\n- James II and VII was born on 14 October 1633 and died on 16 September 1701.\n- From 6 February 1685 until the Glorious Revolution of 1688, James II and VII ruled as King of England and Ireland as James II and as King of Scotland as James VII.\n- The third Viscount Barnewall, who was Nicholas Barnewall's grandson, supported James II and was outlawed.\n- Patrick Barnewall belonged to a junior branch of the Lord Trimlestown family.\n- Patrick Barnewall's descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a3f7635c-6446-5ffe-9952-131aba71e887",
        "text": "Page: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: It was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall, who had earlier represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\nPage: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: His grandson, the third Viscount, was a supporter of James II and outlawed.\nPage: James II of England. Sentence: James II and VII (14 October 1633 – 16 September 1701) was King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII, from 6 February 1685 until he was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688.\nPage: Patrick Barnewall (Solicitor General). Sentence: He belonged to a junior branch of the family of Lord Trimlestown: his own descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.",
